{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/378350-what-are-the-best-homebrewed-dragon-blooded-charms","id":378350,"title":"What are the best homebrewed Dragon-Blooded Charms?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-22T13:58:00-08:00","id":378350,"title":"What are the best homebrewed Dragon-Blooded Charms?","content":"In preparation for a future Dragon-Blooded game set in Ollantijaya, I'm making a unified DB Charm document that puts all the Charms and errata in one place, and having finished that I'm adding some (clearly marked) homebrew Charms there so there's a nice, wide selection. I already have <i>Hundredfold Facets of Enlightenment</i>, <i>Ever-Cascading Torrent of Glory</i>, the <i>Book of Ten Thousand Scorpions</i>, the <i>Perfected Lotus III</i>, a downloaded copy of the old Exalted wiki, and a couple random bits here and there, but I'm curious if there's a major collection of good stuff elsewhere that I'm missing.<br /> <br /> I realize this is pretty subjective, but most of my experience is in 1e and I'm curious if there's any kind of consensus on good fan-made material that I was out of the loop for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: I should mention that by &quot;best&quot; here, I mean least likely to break everything and most interesting from the perspective of Dragon-Blooded as elementally-themed heroes who exist as part of a family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Before enlightenment: chop wood, carry water. After enlightenment: Glorious Tree-Felling Prana and All-Encompassing Liquid-Carrying Methodology.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1223-dorchadas","name":"Dorchadas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1223_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T14:09:28-08:00","id":378378,"title":"","content":"The best homebrew Charms period are anything by The Demented One, aka freelancer Robert Vance. This is an objective truth.<br /> <br /> EDIT: you have Hundredfold Facets listed already - Plague of Hats is also a great homebrewer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 01-22-2015, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T15:17:34-08:00","id":378416,"title":"","content":"I came up with one a few years ago for ride, it let you stick your hands into an expression of your element and drag a mount out of it. So a smokey fire horse, an ever crashing wave, a beasital autumn monster of leaves and twigs, ect. If I remember any more I'll post them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T15:19:38-08:00","id":378422,"title":"","content":"Obviously I'm biased, but you can find mine <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TMcVNd0NGNm_2x_avBHfRkk-X3mmoFpN8PbSqoKXqMY/edit\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> These are the ones I have written up for my most recent game, I have more kicking around somewhere.<br /> <br /> Be careful with those homebrew compilations you mention, they were written for 2e and some of their Charms are redundant or otherwise wonky in 2.5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 01-22-2015, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T15:24:55-08:00","id":378424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/378350-what-are-the-best-homebrewed-dragon-blooded-charms?p=378422#post378422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously I'm biased, but you can find mine <a href=\"https://doc